WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.303
Anger boils over into violent

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.671
protests at the world's

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.740
largest iPhone factory

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.575
worker stream out of Foxconn's

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.510
factory dorms in Central China.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.479
Ho, ho.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:14.381
Protesting unfair treatment,

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:15.015
dirty living

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.783
conditions and chaotic COVID

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.352
rules at the Apple supplier.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.754
Videos obtained by CNN

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.088
show a group of police

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.690
in white hazmat suits

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.691
beating workers

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.627
with batons and metal rods.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.295
The police are hitting people.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.998
A worker shouts in the video.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:32.732
A Foxconn

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.968
employee at the protest told CNN

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.371
the scene turned into a river of blood.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.240
Police hit the workers

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.741
ruthlessly shortly,

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.176
which occurred earlier.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.578
Squadrons of riot police had roll death.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.815
They're going to start beating us.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.784
Protesters yelled in fear,

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:51.484
facing off

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.087
rows of law enforcement with riot gear.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.191
The protest escalated into the evening.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.693
Workers tearing down covered barriers

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.196
using metal beams against police

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:04.831
boxes of

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:05.565
them, hurling

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.801
metal parts towards law enforcement,

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.470
even using a COVID barrier

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.106
as a shield against rows of authorities.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:14.874
They worked together

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.543
to push over a police car,

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.012
cheering and chanting.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:19.979
Since October,

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:20.980
the Foxconn plant

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.148
has been sealed off

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.383
from the outside world

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.051
after a COVID outbreak

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.853
that forced employees to live

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.621
and work on site

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.956
In what videos obtained by

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:30.890
CNN show

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.692
are filthy conditions,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.694
garbage piling up in the hallway.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.797
The factory plunged into chaos.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:38.698
Videos

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:39.432
showed workers

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.633
scrambling, fighting

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.635
to get enough food and supplies.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.537
Then came the exodus.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:45.705
Masses of workers

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:46.573
walked miles

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:47.340
along highways

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.742
to escape the plant Analysts

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.578
estimate this factory produces

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.713
more than half of Apple's iPhones.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.748
Apple already warned customers

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.684
they'll need to wait even longer

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.952
to get their new products

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.321
because of China's COVID lockdowns.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.889
So to attract workers,

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.391
Foxconn promised higher pay and bonuses.

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.627
New workers signed up.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.362
But when they got to the factory,

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.964
the pay package was worse

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:13.266
than what Foxconn advertised.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.201
Tamika NGO Play piano.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.603
A Foxconn employee, said

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.004
workers felt cheated,

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.172
leading to thousands

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.241
of people protesting.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.142
Foxconn later

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:22.976
blamed the payment

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.712
discrepancy on a, quote, technical error

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.714
and sent text messages to workers

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:28.148
offering

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:31.618
to pay them $1,400 to quit and go.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.453
Soon after video

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:33.853
showed

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.288
long lines of workers

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.724
boarding busses to leave the factory.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.992
Their departure

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.860
possibly putting an end to another

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.662
violent and dramatic scene,

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.965
but increasing the pressure on Apple.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.468
It's just the latest victim of China's

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.337
zero COVID policy.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:53.973
Since the city,

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.808
the place where that factory is located,

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:56.609
they've just announced

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.111
they're going to be lifting the lockdown.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.646
But that's not going to immediately

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.314
reverse the damage for Apple

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.249
and the damage is huge.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.317
Analysts are estimating

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:04.918
it was costing

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:05.652
Apple roughly

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.154
$1,000,000,000 a week in lost

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:08.821
iPhone sales.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.455
Erin.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.769
And after Selena's report,

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.204
I want to bring you more now

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.605
of our conversation earlier

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.272
with how

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.174
he is from the eastern part of China.

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.043
He is now studying in England.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:30.843
And this is an interview

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.078
you'll see only here.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.980
I began by asking him about his family

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.148
who are still in China.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:37.217
I asked whether he's worried about them.

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.184
Here's his response.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.454
Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.121
Worried about them

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:42.822
because

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.391
I think I still need to do something

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.060
because some

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.561
some people in China,

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.063
they are protesting against

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:50.630
the government.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.232
So they are taking a much more

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.933
much bigger risk of them.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.634
So

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:56.903
even if I

00:03:56.903 --> 00:04:00.473
I am worried that I have to do this.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.710
When you say you have to do this,

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:06.512
what made you decide to actually protest

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:10.383
my peace and I have to have

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.718
my duty to,

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:14.120
like do something to call

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.056
for their human rights and a normal life

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.792
for the people in China.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.894
Have you spoken to your friends

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:24.197
who are in China and are they scared?

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.833
They are mostly worried

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.002
about what will happen

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.104
after these protests

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:33.306
and after the lockdown

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.508
because the Chinese government

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.277
is imposing

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:40.847
restrictions even harder on this,

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:44.417
on the control of the speech of assembly

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:46.953
and on demonstration.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.388
Some people were arrested

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:51.724
during the protests and

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:54.193
the much more was is they are

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.963
randomly checking the polls,

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.731
posing the citizens

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:01.801
to hand handling their phones.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.503
They do not

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.772
respect the human rights of privacy

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:08.041
and liberty.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.476
You experience the lockdown in Shanghai

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.444
at university.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.111
I know before

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.546
you moved to England for school

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.214
and I know they told you

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.215
how that the lockdown

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.617
there would be six to seven days,

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.352
but it ended up being three months.

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.087
And some of the details

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:23.289
of what you experienced are really hard

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.491
and frankly incredible. To imagine.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.893
Can you tell us about things

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:28.594
like using the bathroom

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.096
and about the food

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.432
and in the lockdown, the Shanghai,

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.468
the all access to Shanghai is control

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.537
or are controlled by the government,

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.205
which means you

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:41.808
any any one that wants to transfer

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.609
some resources like the food,

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.712
like the vegetables, meat,

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:47.780
they have to get the

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.749
official permit permission

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:50.750
from the government

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.819
that the food we are receiving,

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:54.253
we received like is

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:56.089
most us

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:59.892
many times we eat some very, very bad

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:04.063
and some from my meters like stomachache

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.699
or from there some box

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:08.901
and the food's in the air

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.770
and there are some

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.638
residents receiving

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:13.606
the the bad

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:14.941
vegetables, the back meats

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:18.244
and even some received none of them

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:19.579
they are starving at home

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:22.115
and even someone like they died

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:24.817
because of the starving so it's very bad.

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.953
And also like

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.123
in the restrictions and the lockdown,

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:33.059
we we talked all night at the beginning.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:36.829
We played cop games 15 days.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.298
But after those days we are like

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:41.667
we don't want to.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:42.335
So anything

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:44.003
we just lie down

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:47.507
in the bath and staring at the ceiling

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:48.875
wasting our time

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:50.343
because our

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:53.713
our spirit is actually exhausted.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:54.947
How the world

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.282
is watching these protests now

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:57.683
and wondering how big

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:58.317
this will get

00:06:58.317 --> 00:06:59.719
and whether this is about more

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:01.921
than just zero COVID,

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.089
whether it's about freedom

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.657
in a bigger sense.

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:06.426
What do you think of Xi

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:08.461
Jinping's leadership?

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:11.330
I think it's a continuous

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.634
dictatorship of the country

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:17.670
because there are many people are not

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:20.106
comfortable and

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:20.873
agree with him,

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:24.043
but no one can just maybe say

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.812
they spoke out.

00:07:25.812 --> 00:07:26.345
It's a big

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:28.080
that they don't like him

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.850
because if you do, you might be monitored

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.885
and maybe you will be arrested.

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:34.887
Maybe you are in custody.

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:38.057
It's like a control of your liberty.

